  "result": "I've written the revised record for NRS_484B_210_2 to `record.jsonl`. The gate hasn't been re-run on it yet.\n\n**Cause.** The `blind` scenario hid only `rel.bearing` and expected `unknown`. Core never makes that relation unknown this way. When a source doesn't supply `rel.bearing`, Core computes it from the vehicles' positions and headings, so the pass is still decided and the rule came out `compliant`. The coder traced this to `rel_bearing`/`relFrame` in `Core/Vocab/Atoms.lean` and to `Mask.scene` in `Core/Runtime/Manifest.lean`.\n\n**Changes in the record:**\n- **`blind` scenario:** it now hides `kin.position` together with the three relations the rule reads that are computed from positions: `rel.bearing`, `rel.longitudinal_overlap` and `rel.contact`. With no positions, the pass-on-the-right concept and the conflict check (contact and closest approach) can't be decided, so the verdict should be `unknown`. Every unknown should come from a hidden atom, which the gate requires. The narrative is rewritten to match.\n- **Obligation wording:** the prose said the duty runs \"from its beginning\", but the occasion's under-way justification says \"after its beginning\". It now reads \"from the first observation after its beginning\", which is what the coder implemented.\n- **Under-way justification:** \"exceeding b's along its heading\" now reads \"along the subject's own direction of travel\". That matches the coder's rule, which compares velocities because `kin.heading` is not claimed.\n\nEverything else is unchanged: span mappings, the safety standard's reading, parameters and the other three scenarios.\n\n**Remaining risk:** `kin.position` is hidden but not listed among the record's own atoms. It is read through the `drv.interaction.overtake_pass_on_right` concept, whose atoms count as the rule's own. If the gate still requires hidden atoms to be the record's own, `blind` will be refused again.\n\nThe coder's witness file still sets `blind` up with the old hidden list (`[\"rel.bearing\"]`). That entry needs updating to the new list.",
